# Line endings are the repo's decision, not each machine's.
#
# Without this, Windows' default core.autocrlf=true checks out CRLF while the repo stores LF,
# so anything that writes LF - rsync from WSL, a generator run under Linux, most editors -
# makes the entire tree look modified. Pinning it here fixes it for every clone rather than
# per developer.
#
# No .bat/.cmd in this tree; add an `eol=crlf` carve-out if that ever changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

docs/configurator.html text eol=lf
ci_tooling/generate/gen_configurator.py text eol=lf
# Shell scripts must keep LF or the shebang breaks on Linux/WSL/macOS.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The git hooks are executed directly by git and are extensionless, so the *.sh rule above does
# not reach them. Checked out with CRLF they die on Linux/WSL with
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# which silently disables every auto-format step for anyone on a non-Windows clone.
tools/git-hooks/** text eol=lf
